#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf/corr_3pcf.rst:2
msgid "Standard 3PCF"
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf/corr_3pcf.rst:4
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"``Corr_3PCF`` measures the angular three-point correlation function for a"
" triangle with fixed sides :math:`r_{12}` and :math:`r_{13}`. It "
"evaluates the two displaced vertices as window-filtered fields, samples "
"their product around a set of primary vertices, and averages over random "
"rotations. This is the direct-angular counterpart of the harmonic "
"estimator described in :doc:`../corr_3pcf_multipole/corr_3pcf_multipole`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf/corr_3pcf.rst:11
msgid ""
"The public tutorial is ``examples/notebooks/corr3pcf.ipynb``. Its "
"standard 3PCF sections compare the two centre strategies and show how the"
" saved count-level products assemble into :math:`\\zeta` and the reduced "
"statistic :math:`Q`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf/corr_3pcf.rst:17
msgid "Triangle convention"
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf/corr_3pcf.rst:19
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The primary vertex is labelled 1. The two fixed sides are "
":math:`r_{12}=|\\mathbf{x}_2-\\mathbf{x}_1|` and "
":math:`r_{13}=|\\mathbf{x}_3-\\mathbf{x}_1|`; the angular coordinate is "
"either :math:`\\theta` or :math:`\\mu=\\cos\\theta`. The third side "
"follows from"
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf/corr_3pcf.rst:24
#, python-brace-format
msgid "r_{23}^2=r_{12}^2+r_{13}^2-2r_{12}r_{13}\\mu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf/corr_3pcf.rst:28
msgid ""
"For every angular sample, PyHermes rotates this triangle ``n_rot`` times."
" The rotation average is Monte Carlo: increasing ``n_rot`` reduces "
"orientation noise but increases runtime approximately linearly."
msgstr ""

